# Index of the table-driven fault-injection harness, safety_gate_fault_matrix.rs.
#
#   case     | <id> | <section> | <covers,...> | <invariant asserted>
#   delegate | <section> | <covers,...> | <path>::<test fn>   (an existing sweep injects there)
#   exempt   | <section, Enum::Variant or seam:name> | <reason>
#
# <section> is a "### 2.N" rule or the "## 3" durability model of SAFETY_INVARIANTS.md.
# .github/checks/check-safety-gate-matrix.py fails when a section, a variant of a watched
# failpoint or refusal enum, or a test-injection seam has no row.
#
# Real-OS and hardware acceptance stays manual and is not in this table: a power cut on a real
# volume, Windows/macOS permission semantics, a packaged-app restart, a deployed coordination
# service (device supersede, cloned old database).

