case | manifest.tampered_body | 2.10 |  | A manifest changed after signing fails the signature check; the genuine one verifies
case | manifest.unknown_key | 2.10 |  | A manifest signed under an unknown key id is refused; the genuine one verifies
case | manifest.wrong_schema | 2.10 |  | A correctly signed manifest of another schema is refused as a schema error, not a signature error
# ---- 3 durability model: block store, namespace, volume, generation files ----
case | block_commit.BeforeAppend | 3 | CommitPoint::BeforeAppend,seam:arm_commit_fault_for_tests,seam:arm_fault | A crash at BeforeAppend never leaves the index naming a block that is not durable; committed blocks survive; the group is all-or-nothing; writes work after recovery
case | block_commit.AfterSegmentStaged | 3 | CommitPoint::AfterSegmentStaged,seam:arm_commit_fault_for_tests,seam:arm_fault | A crash at AfterSegmentStaged never leaves the index naming a block that is not durable; committed blocks survive; the group is all-or-nothing; writes work after recovery
case | block_commit.AfterSegmentPublished | 3 | CommitPoint::AfterSegmentPublished,seam:arm_commit_fault_for_tests,seam:arm_fault | A crash at AfterSegmentPublished never leaves the index naming a block that is not durable; committed blocks survive; the group is all-or-nothing; writes work after recovery
case | block_commit.MidRecordAppend | 3 | CommitPoint::MidRecordAppend,seam:arm_commit_fault_for_tests,seam:arm_fault | A crash at MidRecordAppend never leaves the index naming a block that is not durable; committed blocks survive; the group is all-or-nothing; writes work after recovery
case | block_commit.AfterAppendBeforeFsync | 3 | CommitPoint::AfterAppendBeforeFsync,seam:arm_commit_fault_for_tests,seam:arm_fault | A crash at AfterAppendBeforeFsync never leaves the index naming a block that is not durable; committed blocks survive; the group is all-or-nothing; writes work after recovery
case | block_commit.AfterFsyncBeforeIndex | 3 | CommitPoint::AfterFsyncBeforeIndex,seam:arm_commit_fault_for_tests,seam:arm_fault | A crash at AfterFsyncBeforeIndex never leaves the index naming a block that is not durable; committed blocks survive; the group is all-or-nothing; writes work after recovery
case | block_commit.DuringIndexTransaction | 3 | CommitPoint::DuringIndexTransaction,seam:arm_commit_fault_for_tests,seam:arm_fault | A crash at DuringIndexTransaction never leaves the index naming a block that is not durable; committed blocks survive; the group is all-or-nothing; writes work after recovery
case | block_commit.AfterIndexCommitBeforeReceipt | 3 | CommitPoint::AfterIndexCommitBeforeReceipt,seam:arm_commit_fault_for_tests,seam:arm_fault | A crash at AfterIndexCommitBeforeReceipt never leaves the index naming a block that is not durable; committed blocks survive; the group is all-or-nothing; writes work after recovery
case | block_commit.DuringRollover | 3 | CommitPoint::DuringRollover,seam:arm_commit_fault_for_tests,seam:arm_fault | A crash at DuringRollover never leaves the index naming a block that is not durable; committed blocks survive; the group is all-or-nothing; writes work after recovery
case | ns_failpoint.AfterStage | 3 | NsFailpoint::AfterStage,seam:arm_failpoint | A stop at AfterStage leaves the target as the whole old or the whole new file; a retry publishes the new one
case | ns_failpoint.BeforeMove | 3 | NsFailpoint::BeforeMove,seam:arm_failpoint | A stop at BeforeMove leaves the target as the whole old or the whole new file; a retry publishes the new one
case | ns_failpoint.AfterMove | 3 | NsFailpoint::AfterMove,seam:arm_failpoint | A stop at AfterMove leaves the target as the whole old or the whole new file; a retry publishes the new one
case | ns_failpoint.AfterDiscardBeforeUnlink | 3 | NsFailpoint::AfterDiscardBeforeUnlink,seam:arm_failpoint | A committed removal whose unlink was skipped is retained under its ledgered name with its bytes; recovery removes it
case | ns_probe.unknown_volume | 3 | UnavailableReason::Unknown | A volume the probe cannot judge is refused as Unknown with nothing created; once reachable it gets a verdict
delegate | 3 | UnavailableReason::GateClosed | crates/yadorilink-fs-platform/src/durable_dir/tests.rs::a_closed_gate_refusal_names_its_cause
exempt | UnavailableReason::VolumeWithoutGuidPath | Reachable only on a Windows volume that has a DOS path but no volume GUID path; the refusal is produced by the Windows volume query and covered by the Windows durability evidence runs, which are manual real-OS acceptance
case | access_denied.publish | 3 |  | A publish into a directory the user may not write is refused with PermissionDenied and leaves no residue; retry after the mode is restored publishes the whole file
case | access_denied.remove | 3 |  | A removal in a directory the user may not write is refused and the file is intact; retry after the mode is restored removes it
case | volume.observe_fails | 3 | VolumeMatch::Same | A failed volume observation is an error to retry, never a weaker identity
case | volume.other_disk | 3 | VolumeMatch::Other | A folder on another identified volume is refused (Other); back on the recorded disk it is Same
case | volume.recorded_unknown | 3 | VolumeMatch::Unconfirmed | A folder whose recorded volume has no stable identity needs the user to re-adopt it; an unknown volume never matches itself
case | volume.observed_unknown | 3 | VolumeMatch::Unconfirmed | A folder now on a volume with no stable identity waits for the user; re-adoption on an identified volume is Same
case | disk_pressure.admission_line | 3 |  | A write that lands exactly on the headroom line is refused; one byte more room admits it
case | disk_pressure.hysteresis | 3 |  | The waiting-for-space state does not clear while free space hovers just above the line; it clears above the resume margin
case | generation.torn_newest | 3 |  | A torn newest generation is never read as the clean latest record; the older complete generation is kept; the next publish recovers
case | generation.unreadable_newest | 3 |  | An unreadable newest generation makes the record unproven (Invalid), never a first run; the next publish recovers
case | generation.resurrected_after_retirement | 3 |  | A retired record stays retired when an old generation comes back; a new publish revives it
